+# BUG-036: the review guard counts release B's builder rounds as Review B rounds
+
+## Objective
+Fix the following confirmed defect: repair the named cause and nothing else. Root cause: when an increment has no rounds record, `_seed_rounds` in `bridge/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py` seeds as many replied Review B rounds as the highest `<N>` of the tracked `handoff/<ID>-r<N>[letter]-report.md` files (`_report_file_rounds`). Since release 2026.10.11d every builder round writes such a report, so under release B the guard counts builder rounds as Review B rounds. Evidence: release B's trial on another project (2026-10-30). The installed guard (release 2026.10.30a) refused an increment's first Review B with `review-guard: refused - round 1 is off the count (current 3)`. That increment, BUG-004 there, had three builder rounds, each sent back by Review A before any Review B. Its first Review B could only be named `-r4`, which is above the three-round ceiling, so it could never reach its cross-family review. With one builder round, the first snapshot is refused `round 1 is reviewed: write <ID>-r2`. The mechanism, in the code at HEAD: `load_rounds` (line 577) seeds a missing `rounds-<ID>.json` through `_seed_rounds` (lines 529-552), which takes `max(letter_n, report_n)` and writes rounds 1..n with `"reply": 0` and `"seeded": True`. `snapshot_review_refusal` (lines 642-706) then treats every seeded round as counted (line 673, "off the count") and as reviewed (lines 675-683, a round with a reply). The governing text says the guard counts Review B rounds, never builder rounds. Merge-Verification-Policy.md says "review-guard.py, which counts the Review B rounds". `bridge/cursor-bridge/workflow/phases/delegation-loop.md` step 8 says "<N> the round it opens: one more than the rounds the guard has counted for the increment". delegation-loop/decide.md, "The review ceiling", says the guard's count and the launcher's count "move independently". Report files are seeded only to cover an increment already in flight when release B was installed. See CHANGELOG 2026.10.30a, Running projects must ("the ID's first snapshot seeds it"), and docs/INVENTORY.md, the R-042 row ("seeds an increment in flight from its letter snapshots and report files"). Reproduction: `tests/test_bug036.py`, written by the supervisor before your run. All 3 of its tests fail on the current tree and must pass: `test_bug036_three_builder_rounds_under_release_b_open_review_round_one`, `test_bug036_one_builder_round_under_release_b_first_snapshot_is_round_one` and `test_bug036_rounds_before_the_install_still_seeded_rounds_after_it_not`. Read the file whole before you start. It imports its helpers from `tests/test_task032_supervisor_guard.py`.
+
+Satisfies: R-042, the code gate's round ceiling held by programs. The clause concerned (docs/REQUIREMENTS.md, the R-042 row): "an increment in flight when the release installs is counted from its snapshots and its builder reports". The guard's count is "the guard's count of rounds opened for the increment", meaning the Review B reads that `review-guard.py snapshot <ID>-r<N>` opens.
+
+## Scope
+One brief carries one increment's scope; work that needs a second scope is a second brief, never a second section here.
+Files and directories you may create or modify:
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py
+- docs/BUILDER_NOTES.md
+- handoff/BUG-036-r1-report.md
+
+Do not modify anything else.
+
+## Out of scope
+- .env and anything under secrets/
+- CI configuration
+- docs/ and handoff/, except the files the Scope section names. The governance texts (Merge-Verification-Policy.md, the workflow phase modules, docs/INVENTORY.md, docs/REQUIREMENTS.md, docs/CHANGES.md, docs/debug/) are the supervisor's.
+- every file under tests/. Above all, `tests/test_bug036.py` is the supervisor's reproduction: it goes from red to green and is never edited.
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge_env.py and bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge-run.py
+- bridge/cursor-bridge/MANIFEST.json, bridge/cursor-bridge/VERSION and bridge/cursor-bridge/CHANGELOG.md: the stamp is the supervisor's step after your run. Do not run `tools/make-manifest.py` or `tools/dump-cli.py`.
+- in review-guard.py: the module docstring, `_seed_refuse_snapshots`, `_snapshot_counts_for_id`, `_letter_snapshot_rounds`, `load_rounds`, `write_rounds`, `snapshot_review_refusal` and every other function except `_report_file_rounds` and `_seed_rounds`. The command line does not change.
+
+## Context
+All paths are relative to the Workspace root (the folder you were started in).
+
+- **Development data** (docs/INVENTORY.md, Decisions): "the dev build is the Workspace sources under `bridge/`; a session in the repo always runs the *installed* bridge (`~/.claude`), never the one being edited, and installs reach running projects only through the owner's install run sheet". What this means for you: never run `review-guard.py`, `bridge-run.py` or the installed bridge against this Workspace or any real checkout. A snapshot would write into this repository's git common dir. Never touch `~/.claude` or `~/.cursor-bridge`. The tests build throwaway git repositories under pytest's `tmp_path` and run the guard there. Run only the commands named in Done.
+- **Security:** ASVS level 2 (docs/INVENTORY.md: "The builder's secure-coding rule is ASVS level 2"). `.cursor/rules/secure-coding.mdc` is in force. Trust boundary: the launcher log `run/launcher/runs.jsonl` and the tracked file names under `handoff/` are inputs the guard reads. A row of the log is untrusted: `bridge_env.read_runs_jsonl` already drops rows whose `brief` is not a string or whose `round` is not an int (`bridge_env._valid_log_row`). This guard is a safety mechanism. The fix must not let anything other than a release-B builder row of the same ID and round lower the seed.
+- There is no docs/DESIGN.md. The design is stated here, in the governance texts quoted in the Objective, and in `tests/test_bug036.py`'s docstring.
+- **Host:** no behaviour of this increment depends on the host (Claude Code). The guard is a one-shot program run from the shell. The supervisor's session runs inside the Claude desktop app, which puts no `claude` command on PATH, so no `claude --version` is recorded. No in-host test applies.
+
+The two functions the cause lives in, as at HEAD on branch bug-036 (`bridge/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py`; `re`, `json`, `os` and `bridge_env` are already imported):
+
+```python
+def _report_file_rounds(root, common, id_part):
+    try:
+        out = run_git(["ls-files", "handoff/"], root, common)
+    except RuntimeError:
+        return 0
+    lines = out.splitlines()
+    pat = re.compile(r"^handoff/%s-r(\d+)[a-z]?-report\.md$" % re.escape(id_part))
+    best = 0
+    for line in lines:
+        m = pat.match(line.replace("\\", "/"))
+        if m:
+            best = max(best, int(m.group(1)))
+    return best
+
+
+def _seed_rounds(common, root, id_part):
+    refuse = _seed_refuse_snapshots(common, id_part)
+    if refuse:
+        return None, refuse
+    letter_n, branch = _letter_snapshot_rounds(common, root, id_part)
+    report_n = _report_file_rounds(root, common, id_part)
+    n = max(letter_n, report_n)
+    ...   # rounds 1..n: {"round", "name", "branch", "tree": "", "time": "", "lift": None, "reply": 0, "seeded": True}
+    return {"id": id_part, "rounds": rounds}, None
+```
+
+The launcher log is read the way the guard already reads it in `snapshot_review_refusal`:
+
+```python
+log_folder = bridge_env.launcher_log_folder(common, root)
+# bridge_env.read_runs_jsonl(log_folder) -> list of dict rows (malformed lines and rows skipped)
+```
+
+The shape of the builder row is in `bridge/cursor-bridge/bridge-run.py`, read-only for you. `builder_review_refusal` returns meta with `"brief": id_part` and `"round": name_round`. Here `name_round` is the round of the brief's own name: 1 for `<ID>.md`, N for `<ID>-r<N>.md`, which is the same `<N>` the builder's report file `<ID>-r<N>-report.md` carries. `main()` then calls `entry.update(brief=..., round=..., brief_sha256=..., brief_name=..., lift=..., merge_ids=...)` only when that meta exists. For `kind == "review"` the meta is `None`, so a review row carries no `brief`. The earlier launcher wrote neither `brief` nor `round`. The test fixture `launcher_line` in `tests/test_task032_supervisor_guard.py` (line 232) writes such a row exactly as the launcher does.
+
+The test that pins the in-flight case, which must keep passing unchanged: `tests/test_task032_supervisor_guard.py::test_task032_guard_r14_five_report_files_outrank_two_snapshots`. It has five report files and two letter snapshots, logs no builder row, and seeds five rounds.
+
+## Diagrams
+None: no diagram under docs/diagrams/ covers the review guard.
+
+## Requirements
+1. A release-B builder row for a report `handoff/<ID>-r<N>[letter]-report.md` is a row of `bridge_env.read_runs_jsonl(bridge_env.launcher_log_folder(common, root))` that meets all three of: `kind` equal to `"builder"`; `brief` equal to the ID (`id_part`); `round` an int (not a bool) equal to that report's `<N>`. A row matches whatever its `exit`, `healthy`, `branch`, `brief_name` or other fields are.
+2. A report file counts toward the seed only if its round has no release-B builder row. The seed from report files is the highest `<N>` among the tracked report files whose round has no such row, or 0 if there are none.
+3. Everything else in the seed stays exactly as it is: the letter-snapshot count (`_letter_snapshot_rounds`), `n = max(letter_n, report_n)`, the refusals of `_seed_refuse_snapshots` and their order (they still come first), the tracked-file listing and its pattern (letter suffixes included), and the seeded entries' shape (`reply` 0, `seeded` True, `tree` "", `time` "", `lift` None, the names and branch as today). Every other rule of the guard is unchanged.
+4. As a result, an increment whose builder rounds all ran under release B seeds nothing from its reports, and its first Review B is round 1 under its bare name or `-r1`. An increment in flight at an install, built before it, seeds as it does today. A mixed increment seeds only the rounds built before the install. A builder row of another ID never affects this ID's seed.
+5. A missing or unreadable launcher log means no release-B rows: every report counts, as today. No new refusal, exit code or output line is added.
+6. Neither function carries a comment or docstring today. You may add one short comment at `_report_file_rounds` or `_seed_rounds` stating the rule ("a report counts only for a round with no release-B builder row"). Add nothing longer.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
