+- [ ] `tests/test_task032_supervisor_guard.py` (including `test_task032_guard_r14_five_report_files_outrank_two_snapshots`), `tests/test_task032_supervisor_r4.py` and the other test files that name review-guard pass unchanged, as run by Done step 3.
+- [ ] The cause is addressed at its mechanism: `_seed_rounds` no longer counts a report file whose round the release-B launcher logged as a builder row of the same ID, so a builder round is never seeded as a replied Review B round. Report files from before the install still seed as before.
+- [ ] `git diff --stat` shows only `bridge/cursor-bridge/review-guard.py`, `docs/BUILDER_NOTES.md` (if you appended) and `handoff/BUG-036-r1-report.md`. In review-guard.py the diff touches only `_report_file_rounds` and `_seed_rounds`, plus at most a new private helper beside them.
+- [ ] `git diff --quiet HEAD -- tests/` exits 0 (no tracked test file changed), and `tests/test_bug036.py` is byte-identical to the file you found.
+- [ ] Every requirement under "Satisfies" is fully met for this cause, with no stand-in or placeholder. The trace to R-042 is carried by the supervisor's `tests/test_bug036.py` docstrings, so you add no test.
+- [ ] No new Semgrep high findings. All output stays ASCII-only.
+
+## Constraints
